(i) Prop 2.1: matched against the companion "Routing densities" Cor 6.2 (strong pointwise smoothing). It covers both orientations, every coordinate order and all 0≤l≤N, as cited.
(ii) Sparse rows, Prop 3.1:
- the polar deformation Y(z)=W|Y|^{p0 z/2}, and the entry bound sqrt((|Y|^a)_xx(|Y*|^a)_yy) via |Y*|^{a/2}W|Y|^{a/2};
- monotonicity p0/2≥2u, and exactness of single-card lines;
- unique intermediate paths, the bound K≤n^{-q}e^U, and the HS² bound through the Markov kernel;
- U≤gR_*, and the connected-set and sampling-without-replacement estimate under the hypothesis (q/n)e^{C2√log n}≤½;
- three-lines interpolation at θ=2/p0;
- q=k(n/k)^{1/5} with q²/n=k(k/n)^{3/5};
- the skew-tableau multiplicity binom(q,k)D_β, the hook formula (13), m_λ≥D^{1/10}, and summation of the tails over k≤√n and k>√n.
